BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Michael Massie | now and then Curatorial Tour with Alysa Procida
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270120T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270120T170000
UID:michael-massie-now-and-then-curatorial-tour-alysa-procida@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join exhibition guest curator Alysa Procida for an in-depth cu
 ratorial tour of Michael Massie | now and then\n\nMichael Massie | now and
  then Curatorial Tour with Alysa Procida – Wednesday\, January 20\, 2027
 \, 4 p.m. to 5 p.m.\, Onsite Gallery\, 199 Richmond Street West Discover t
 he ideas behind Michael Massie | now and then in a special curator-led tou
 r with exhibition guest curator Alysa Procida. Through an engaging\, in-de
 pth discussion\, Alysa will explore the exhibition’s curatorial vision a
 nd the creative evolution of Michael Massie’s remarkable practice. Spann
 ing the breadth of Massie’s career\, Michael Massie | now and then bring
 s together an extraordinary collection of works\, including his celebrated
  teapots\, previously unexhibited pieces\, and a striking new series of la
 rge-scale sculptural installations. This tour offers a unique opportunity 
 to gain deeper insight into the stories\, themes\, and artistic vision tha
 t shape one of the exhibition’s most compelling contemporary voices. Abo
 ut the Guest Curator Alysa Procida is an arts administrator\, curator\, an
 d consultant who is passionate about connecting artists with audiences acr
 oss the world. She is the 2026 International Liaison for the Arctic Arts S
 ummit Secretariat\, having previously co-organized the 2022 Arctic Arts Su
 mmit in Whitehorse\, YK. Previously\, she was the Executive Director of th
 e Inuit Art Foundation (IAF) and Publisher of the Inuit Art Quarterly (IAQ
 )\, Chair of the Magazines Canada Board of Directors\, and a mentor on the
  Inuit Futures in Arts Leadership: The Pilimmaksarniq / Pijariuqsarniq Pro
 ject. As Publisher of the IAQ \, Alysa oversaw a full redesign of the maga
 zine in conjunction with the IAF’s 30th anniversary in 2017 and the maga
 zine’s first National Magazine Award in 2018. In 2019\, she was shortlis
 ted for Publisher Grand Prix at the National Magazine Awards\, and in 2021
  the IAQ was awarded Best Arts and Literary Magazine and winner of the Mag
 azine Grand Prix. Registration Page Coming Soon
LOCATION:Onsite Gallery (RHD) 199 Richmond Street West 199 Richmond Street
  West
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-the
 n-curatorial-tour-alysa-procida
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Matriarchal Messages for the Masses
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270105T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270331T235959
UID:matriarchal-messages-masses@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:A community-centred pop-up project initiated by Amy Wong that 
 celebrates the wisdom passed down through mothers\, aunties\, elders\, car
 egivers\, and chosen family.\n\nMMM! Matriarchal Messages for the Masses M
 MM! (Matriarchal Messages for the Masses) is a community-centred pop-up pr
 oject initiated by Amy Wong that celebrates the wisdom passed down through
  mothers\, aunties\, elders\, caregivers\, and chosen family. Through an o
 pen call and poster making workshop\, you are invited to share matriarchal
  messages\, everyday teachings\, reminders\, and words of care. Drawing es
 pecially from 2SLGBTQIA+/BIPOC knowledge traditions\, selected submissions
  will be transformed into a series of collaboratively produced screen-prin
 ted T-shirts and totes. Part wearable tribute\, part living archive\, MMM!
  brings intergenerational knowledge into public space and honours the voic
 es that shape our cultures and communities. About MMM! Monday\, Oct 5\, 11
  AM: MMM! (Matriarchal Messages for the Masses) Project Launch Info sessio
 n on Teams (led by Amy Wong) November 2-6: MMM! Poster Workshop\, Lobby 10
 0 McCaul (led by Amy Wong and Tannis Nielsen\, FOA) January 20 and January
  27\, 2027: Screen printing workshops (led by Amy Wong and Shannon Gerard\
 , FOA) SPOTS ARE LIMITED\; REGISTRATION IS IN THE SIGN UP BELOW Feb 2027 d
 ates TBA: Pop-up shop with proceeds to be donated to support OCADU 150 pro
 gramming\, Sistering and the Barbara Schlifer Commemorative Clinic Sign up
  and join the project: Call for Student Volunteers: MMM! Matriarchal Messa
 ges for the Masses – Fill out form Eligibility: Current OCAD students Si
 gn up by: Friday\, October 16\, 2026\, 12 pm Any questions? Contact: Amy W
 ong\, awong@ocadu.ca
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/matriarchal-messages-masse
 s
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Akin Career Launcher: Info Session & Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T190000
UID:akin-career-launcher-info-session-tour@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for this info-session if you are thinking about applyi
 ng to Akin Career Launcher!\n\nAkin Career Launcher: Info Session & Tour D
 ate/Time: Monday\, December 7\, 2026\, 5:00 - 7:00 p.m. Location: Akin Ric
 hmond Bathurst\, 579 Richmond St W\, Toronto Register to attend Join us fo
 r this info-session if you are thinking about applying to Akin Career Laun
 cher. You will hear from Farah Yusuf\, OCAD U CEAD Special Projects Coordi
 nator\, about the Akin Career Launcher and how to put together a strong ap
 plication. Renato Baldin\, Gallery Manager at Remote Gallery \, will speak
  to the many ways Remote Gallery can be utilized and show some examples fr
 om previous Akin Career Launcher recipients’ exhibitions and events. Cha
 rlotte Van Ryn\, Studio Manager at Akin Richmond-Bathurst \, will give an 
 overview of Akin’s studio locations and memberships\, and lead a studio 
 tour of Akin’s Richmond-Bathurst location after the info session. Access
  Details : Participants will be met by Akin staff in the lobby of 579 Rich
 mond St. W. There is a step on the street level leading into the main foye
 r. Once inside\, there are an additional 9 steps leading up to the elevato
 r. The elevator takes you up to the third and fourth floor. The Akin Studi
 os exist on one level of the building\, with no stairs within the unit. Th
 e private\, gender neutral bathrooms are inside the unit with a 1 inch ste
 p lip leading into each bathroom. Learn more about the 2027 Akin Career La
 uncher Call For Artists
LOCATION:Off Campus Akin Richmond Bathurst\, 579 Richmond St W\, Toronto
URL:https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/YLLn7SCDEg
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
