BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EXPERIENCE CREATE: Sculpting from Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T160000
UID:experience-create-sculpting-life@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Sculpting from Life with Associate Professor Francis LeBouthil
 ler\, part of Alumni Relations' November workshop series.\n\nSculpting fro
 m Life with Associate Professor Francis LeBouthiller Dates: Saturday\, Nov
 ember 28th Location: Room 617 6th Floor\, 100 McCaul St. Time: 12:15pm to 
 1:00pm: Welcome Reception 1:00pm to 4:00pm: Workshop Cost: $30 per person 
 All materials provided In this hands-on workshop\, participants will use r
 aw clay to sculpt from a live model under the guidance of Associate Profes
 sor\, Francis Lebouthillier. Participants should wear comfortable clothes 
 and shoes they don’t mind getting dirty. Francis LeBouthillier is a Toro
 nto-based multi-disciplinary artist\, designer\, researcher and educator. 
 Since 1989\, Francis has been an Associate Professor at OCAD University\, 
 where he teaches in the Faculty of Art. For over 20 years\, Francis has ma
 intained a research practice that involves developing high-fidelity surgic
 al simulators and medical models . This work has involved research teams a
 t Toronto's Mount Sinai Hospital\, Women's College Hospital\, and the Univ
 ersity of Toronto's Surgical Skills Lab.
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street Room 617
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/experience-create-sculptin
 g-life
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
