BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Isabel Meirelles Sabbatical Presentation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T130000
UID:isabel-meirelles-sabbatical-presentation@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join Isabel Meirelles for a presentation examining the rise\, 
 disappearance\, and preservation of early web-based data visualization pro
 jects\n\nDrawing on ongoing research into pioneering digital works from th
 e mid-1990s to the 2010s\, Meirelles explores how designers used emerging 
 web technologies to create innovative forms of visual storytelling and cul
 tural data representation. The talk will consider the challenges of docume
 nting works lost to obsolete platforms and technologies\, highlighting the
  importance of preserving digital design history for future generations of
  designers\, artists\, and researchers. Monday\, November 23\, 2026 12:00-
 1:00 p.m. MCA 570
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street Room 570
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/isabel-meirelles-sabbatica
 l-presentation
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:1976 OCA Punk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T120015
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T170025
UID:1976-oca-punk@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:1976 OCA Punk is a celebratory special event planned for Satur
 day\, November 21\, 2026 at OCAD University\, 100 McCaul street\, Toronto\
 ; and is part of OCAD 150\, the University’s 150 th Anniversary commemor
 ation in 2026.\n\n1976 OCA Punk 1976 OCA Punk is a celebratory special eve
 nt planned for Saturday\, November 21\, 2026 at OCAD University\, 100 McCa
 ul Street\, Toronto\; and is part of OCAD 150\, the University’s 150 th 
 Anniversary commemoration in 2026. Saturday\, November 21\, 2026\, 12 – 
 5 PM Doors open at noon OCAD University\, The Auditorium 100 McCaul St.\, 
 Room 190 Refreshments and beverages are provided (19+ event) No RSVP requi
 red This half day long gathering\, 1976 OCA PUNK\, hosts alumni and friend
 s in the University Auditorium to acknowledge the many student-led bands w
 ho performed at the school during OCA’s Centennial Year in 1976/77\, as 
 well as\, the campus community who supported and collaborated with them ha
 lf a century ago. OCA alumni\, family and friends are invited to reunite i
 n the OCAD Auditorium along with many original members of the historic 1st
  wave art-school punk bands OCA produced in 1976: The Cads\, The Eels\, Oh
  Those Pants\, The Diodes\, Johnny & the G-Rays\, The Curse\, The Concorde
 s\, The Country Lads\, Martha & the Muffins\, and more! The Lost Anglers O
 rchestra will play\, along with some surprise musical guests. Vintage vide
 os and many photographs of OCA alumni and rare musical performances from 5
 0 years ago will be seen — much of it originally shot in the same audito
 rium. Canada's first punk bands return to the scene of their first perform
 ances. There will be a mixture of scheduled and spontaneous activities. Da
 vid Clarkson will make intros and facilitate conversation celebrating the 
 creative achievements of this particularly unique cohort.
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street OCAD University\, The Auditorium 100 McCaul St.\, Room 190
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/1976-oca-punk
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
