BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Attacks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T190000
UID:art-attacks-roundtable-art-punk-and-queen-west-scene-70s-and-80s@ocadu
 .ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Art Attacks: Roundtable On Art\, Punk\, And The Qu
 een West Scene of the 70s And 80s aims to explore the role of Canada’s o
 ldest art school in the underground music that emerged here alongside scen
 es in London and New York.\n\nJoin us for Art Attacks: Roundtable On Art\,
  Punk\, And The Queen West Scene of the 70s And 80s aims to explore the ro
 le of Canada’s oldest art school in the underground music that emerged h
 ere alongside scenes in London and New York. Artist\, programmer\, and OCA
 D U alum Tara Bursey (BFA\, Criticism & Curatorial Practice\, 2013) modera
 tes a conversation with David Clarkson (The Diodes)\, GB Jones (Fifth Colu
 mn\, J.D.s Zine)\, and Don Pyle (Shadowy Men on a Shadowy Planet\, Crash K
 ills Five) about art during punk’s first wave\, what followed\, and its 
 relationship to art education.
LOCATION:Learning Zone 113 McCaul Street Room 110\, Level 1
